    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nuevo means “new” in Spanish, a name that reflects its early settlers’ hope for a fresh start.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuevo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits just east of Lake Perris, tucked into the foothills of the San Jacinto Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuevo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The usually dry San Jacinto River traces the northern edge of Nuevo, shaping its early irrigation practices.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuevo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coastal Sage Scrub dominates Nuevo’s natural vegetation, though much of it now survives only in small patches amid homes and farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
